# Code owners for the owner-merge paths, and nothing else.
#
# GitHub no longer requires code-owner review: the ruleset
# (.github/rulesets/main.json) sets require_code_owner_review to false, by the
# owner's decision of 2026-11-23. What makes these paths need the owner is the
# hive's own merge gate, auto_merge.human_merge_paths, which lists exactly the
# paths below. The hive labels a pull request that touches one of them
# `needs-owner-merge` and leaves the merge to the owner. Every other pull
# request merges on the required check and the hive's AI reviewer.
#
# This file only makes GitHub ask for the owner's review automatically on a pull
# request that touches one of these paths. It gates nothing by itself, so keep
# it the same list as human_merge_paths: tests/test_codeowners.py holds it to
# that list, and fails if a catch-all `*` line comes back.
# docs/branch-protection.md explains the rule.

